<title>NIGERIA: Nigeria's National Oil profit plunges.</title>
<headline>Nigeria's National Oil profit plunges.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996</p>
<p>				(In million naira unless stated)</p>
<p>						   1996		 1995</p>
<p>     Turnover				 14,100   vs 14,600</p>
<p>     Profit before taxation		   344 vs 1,600</p>
<p>     Taxation				     90.6 vs 466.4</p>
<p>     Profit after taxation		    253.4 vs 1,200</p>
<p>Dividend - One naira per share vs 8.35 naira Scrip - One new share for every six scrip is being proposed. NOTE- Owners of National Oil and Chemical Marketing Company are Nigerian National Petroleum Corp (NNPC) (40 percent), Nigerian unit of Royal Dutch Shell Group Nigeria (40 percent) and Nigerian citizens (20 percent).</p>
<p>($1=85 naira)</p>
<p>-- Lagos newsroom +234 1 263 03 17</p>
</text>
